  under the backup path: remove /var/backups/hardn/.write_test (screen)
  after: /var/backups/hardn: a directory, empty
  the temp dir afterwards (recorded, not compared): hardn.yml var/ var/backups/ var/backups/hardn/
new path: item 1, through screenkit.Session.Change: the control's plan, then its apply, on the engine as cmd/hardn builds it
  write /etc/hardn/hardn.yml 0644, atomic
    - enableBackups: true               # Backup files before modifying them
    + enableBackups: false               # Backup files before modifying them
  under the backup path: mkdir /var/backups/hardn/<run id> 0700
  under the backup path: write /var/backups/hardn/<run id>/0001-hardn.yml 0600
  under the backup path: write /var/backups/hardn/<run id>/manifest.json 0600
  after: /var/backups/hardn: a directory holding <run id>
  backup: /etc/hardn/hardn.yml (taken anyway: backups off); journal: journalled first; findings: none
agree  refusal: none
agree  files: none
agree  directories: none
agree  commands: none
agree  findings: none
agree  hardn.yml enableBackups: false
agree  hardn.yml settings: as loaded
differ backupPath dirs: none | /var/backups/hardn/<run id> 0700
       plan §3.16; control-backup.md §2.3: nothing made; now the change's run directory, 0700
differ backupPath files: write /var/backups/hardn/.write_test 0644 (screen), remove /var/backups/hardn/.write_test (screen) | write /var/backups/hardn/<run id>/0001-hardn.yml 0600, write /var/backups/hardn/<run id>/manifest.json 0600
       decision 3; plan §3.16; control-backup.md §2.3; side-effects row 30: the screen's write test on its first draw; now the copy of hardn.yml and the run's manifest, 0600
differ backupPath after: /var/backups/hardn: a directory, empty | /var/backups/hardn: a directory holding <run id>
       plan §3.16: left empty; now holding the change's backup run
differ write: in place | atomic
       plan §3.19: written in place; now replaced whole by a rename
differ backup: none | /etc/hardn/hardn.yml (taken anyway: backups off)
       plan §3.16; decisions 7 (a), 8: nothing backed up; now hardn.yml first, taken anyway with backups off, and said
differ journal: none | journalled first
       control-backup.md §2.8: no rollback; now journalled first, naming the backup run
differ hardn.yml: ./hardn.yml, in the working directory | /etc/hardn/hardn.yml, the file loaded
       side-effects row 29; plan §3.19: ./hardn.yml, last in hardn's search order; now the file loaded
differ hardn.yml rest: 48 settings, written whole; no file was loaded | the enableBackups lines alone changed; the file's other 4 lines kept (4 settings, 1 comment lines)
       side-effects row 29; plan §3.19: every setting written whole; now the enableBackups line alone
v0.3.2: ./hardn.yml saved whole, dryRun included (§4.13, menu 10), nothing checked or made (read: menu.go:728-743); BackupFile then backed up before its 15 writes, unless enableBackups was false (§3; §5.1, V18: regressed)

